{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>By me kings reign</b> — that their kingdom endures, or they are called by the name of their end, as in: 'and she grind for him [grain into] flour.' [n. The allusion is to an instance where a word is predicated by its ultimate outcome rather than its present state; Ibn Ezra's reference to וטחני קמח could not be pinned to a single verse with certainty.]" "<b>and princes decree justice</b> — to decree statutes of just judgment."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "The biblical verse alluded to (וטחני קמח) could not be identified with certainty; the phrase may be corrupt or fragmentary."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:27.002511029Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}